Piper (text to speech) — invoked as a separate process, not linked
------------------------------------------------------------------

  Component : piper-tts
  Upstream  : https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl
  Version   : 1.6.0 (installed 2026-07-25)
  Licence   : GPL-3.0-or-later
              (it bundles/links espeak-ng, which is GPL-3.0-or-later)

**Relationship, stated deliberately.** Piper is NOT a dependency of this
application. It is not in `pyproject.toml`, it is not in `uv.lock`, it is
not installed in the app's virtual environment, and there is no
`import piper` anywhere in `app/`. It lives in its own environment
(`uv tool install piper-tts`) and this application invokes the `piper`
executable as a **separate process** through a configurable command
(`TTS_COMMAND` — see `app/speech.py` and `.env.example`), passing text on
stdin and receiving a WAV file.

That arrangement is the owner's decision of 2026-07-25 and exists for two
reasons, recorded here so nobody removes it as an unnecessary
indirection: the licence relationship above, and the fact that adding
Piper to the app's lockfile would re-resolve its dependency graph — churn
that has corrupted this machine's CUDA wheels before.

Anyone redistributing this project should form their own view of the
licence position rather than relying on this note. Nothing here is legal
advice.


Voice model: en_GB-alba-medium
------------------------------

  Source    : https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices
              (en/en_GB/alba/medium)
  Installed : outside the repository, at the path in TTS_MODEL_PATH.
              The model is ~63 MB and is deliberately NOT committed.

**What the model card actually says**, quoted rather than assumed — the
card records a licence for the *training dataset* and does not state a
separate licence for the model weights:

    # Model card for alba (medium)
    * Language: en_GB (English, Great Britain)
    * Speakers: 1
    * Quality: medium
    * Samplerate: 22,050Hz
    ## Dataset
    * URL: https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/3270
    * License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    ## Training
    * Finetuned from U.S. English lessac voice (medium quality).

So: **dataset CC BY 4.0** (attribution required — the dataset is the
University of Edinburgh CSTR corpus at the datashare URL above), and the
weights' own licence is **not stated on the card**. The gap is recorded
rather than filled in: it is the voice the face study will be run with,
and if this project is ever published the position should be confirmed
with the voice's publisher rather than inferred.


kindalive (Phase 7b — vendored 2026-07-28)
------------------------------------------

  Upstream  : https://github.com/smithandrewjohn/kindalive
  Licence   : MIT (upstream LICENSE kept at vendor/kindalive/LICENSE)
  Pinned    : commit a29bcf73e2c44cbf2fa6549ae28d1a9d1f6f37b6

Vendored by copying files (no dependency added, no lockfile change — the
same arms-length pattern as Piper) per `PHASE_7B_KINDALIVE.md` build
decision 1. What was vendored, all from the pinned commit:

  vendor/kindalive/engine/       chemicals, clock, impulse, interactions,
                                 neurochemical_engine, seed_chemistry
  vendor/kindalive/emotions/     emotion_vector, projection
  vendor/kindalive/expression/   face.py, face_3d.py (setTargets payload
                                 construction lives here, so it was kept),
                                 base.py, __init__.py
  vendor/kindalive/config/       chemicals.toml, emotions.toml, face.toml,
                                 personalities.toml
  app/static/face3d.js           the canvas renderer, copied unchanged
                                 from expression/web_assets/face3d.js

The only modifications to the vendored .py files are import rewrites
(`kindalive.` → `vendor.kindalive.`); `personalities.toml` additionally
carries this project's `[clinical]` preset. The upstream LLM interpreter
(`interpreter/` package) was deliberately NOT vendored — the owner's
decision is to inject impulses deterministically from consultation
events instead (build decision 2).


Clinical guideline corpus
-------------------------

Guideline content is fetched per installation under the operator's own
licences and is never redistributed with this software. It is **never
committed** — the corpus directory is gitignored. `corpus/manifest.yaml` is the
per-installation provenance record of what was fetched and from where; it
is local and uncommitted (like `.env`), and `corpus/manifest.example.yaml`
is the committed example of its format.


